// README.md
# Rust Project Compiler

This library provides utilities for compiling Rust projects and managing a C-based resource loader.

## Installation

Add the following to your `Cargo.toml`:

```toml
[dependencies]
rust_project_compiler = "0.1.0"
```

## Usage

### Compilation Module

```rust
use rust_project_compiler::Compiler;

fn main() {
    let compiler = Compiler::new("path/to/config.toml".to_string());
    match compiler.compile() {
        Ok(exit_code) => println!("Compilation successful, exit code: {}", exit_code),
        Err(e) => eprintln!("Error: {}", e),
    }
}
```

### Resource Loader Module

```rust
use rust_project_compiler::ResourceBundleLoader;

fn main() {
    let loader = ResourceBundleLoader::new();
    match loader.load_bundle(Path::new("path/to/bundle")) {
        Ok(_) => println!("Bundle loaded successfully"),
        Err(e) => eprintln!("Error: {}", e),
    }
}
```

## Contributing

Contributions are welcome! Please read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for details on how to contribute.

